CAT = "nzfaLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Without a firearms licence, you may use a standard firearm only:",
 "Under immediate supervision", ["On private farmland", "For pest control", "With the firearm owner's consent"],
 "Everyone who possesses or uses a firearm needs a licence, though standard firearms can be used under the immediate supervision of a licence holder in most circumstances."),
("\"Immediate supervision\" means the licence holder:",
 "Is close enough to take control", ["Is somewhere on the property", "Can be reached by phone", "Is somewhere in the same hunting party"],
 "The supervisor must be physically present and actively supervising, close enough to take control of the firearm, and not using another firearm."),
("While giving immediate supervision, a licence holder must not:",
 "Use another firearm", ["Give the shooter instructions", "Load the shooter's magazine", "Stand within arm's reach"],
 "A supervisor cannot be using another firearm at the same time. They must be able to take control of the shooter's firearm."),
("To hold a firearms licence, a person must be assessed as:",
 "A fit and proper person", ["A member of a shooting club", "A farmer or landowner", "Aged 25 or over"],
 "A fit and proper person is of good character and can be trusted to use firearms responsibly and store them securely."),
("Which of these people is disqualified from holding a firearms licence?",
 "A gang member", ["A person over 70", "A first-time applicant", "A farm worker"],
 "The Arms Act 2026 makes any person identified as a gang member ineligible for a firearms licence. Close gang affiliation can also mean a person is not fit and proper."),
("Your rifle is stolen from your home. What must you do?",
 "Report it straight away", ["Wait 30 days in case it turns up", "Mention it at licence renewal", "Tell only your insurer"],
 "Report lost or stolen firearms as soon as possible, for example by calling 105 or reporting online, with everything you know about the items and the theft."),
("Selling a rifle face to face, the buyer must:",
 "Hold a valid firearms licence", ["Be aged 21 or over", "Live in your region", "Belong to a local shooting club"],
 "You must sell or supply firearms only to someone with a valid licence (or a licensed business), and take reasonable steps to check it."),
("How can you confirm a buyer's licence card is current?",
 "Use the Firearms Licence Checker", ["Phone one of their licence referees", "Ask for a utility bill", "Check their club card"],
 "The Firearms Licence Checker confirms instantly whether a licence card is current and legitimate. It shows nothing beyond the card details."),
("To possess a pistol, a licence holder needs:",
 "An endorsement and a permit", ["A standard licence only", "A club membership card only", "A 10-year licence"],
 "Pistols, restricted weapons, restricted firearms and restricted magazines need the right endorsement on the licence and an approved permit to possess for each item."),
("For a standard licence holder, a centrefire semi-automatic rifle is:",
 "A restricted firearm", ["Allowed with a small magazine", "Allowed for pest control", "A standard firearm"],
 "Centrefire semi-automatic rifles are restricted firearms under the Arms Act 2026 (prohibited firearms under the 1983 Act). A standard licence holder cannot have or use one without the right endorsement and permit."),
("Fitting a magazine holding more than 10 rounds to a .22 rimfire semi-automatic makes it:",
 "Illegal on a standard licence", ["Legal for target shooting", "Legal on private land", "Legal for rabbit and possum control"],
 "A .22 rimfire semi-automatic is a standard firearm only with a magazine of 10 cartridges or fewer. Fitting a larger magazine puts it outside a standard licence, needing an endorsement and permit."),
("A 16-year-old wants to use an airgun without supervision. They need:",
 "A firearms licence", ["A parent's written consent", "Only private land to use it on", "To use .177 pellets only"],
 "Sixteen and seventeen-year-olds who want to have and use airguns unsupervised need a firearms licence."),
("To possess a high-energy airgun, such as a specified pre-charged pneumatic air rifle, you need:",
 "A firearms licence", ["No licence if you are 18", "A club membership card", "Only the seller's receipt"],
 "Most airguns need no licence for adults, but high-energy airguns (specially dangerous airguns), including specified pre-charged pneumatic air rifles, are treated like firearms and need a firearms licence."),
("When must a licence holder's secure storage be inspected and approved?",
 "Even if they own no firearms", ["Only when they first buy a pistol", "Only after a theft", "Only if they live in a city"],
 "All licence holders must have secure storage inspected and approved, even if they do not yet possess firearms or ammunition."),
("You develop an illness that affects your ability to use firearms safely. You should:",
 "Tell the licensing authority", ["Keep using them with care", "Wait for renewal to mention it", "Store them at a mate's house"],
 "Licence holders must tell the regulator about a physical or mental illness or injury that affects their ability to possess firearms safely, and can arrange to surrender or dispose of them."),
("Carrying a firearm in a public place without a lawful purpose is:",
 "An offence", ["Allowed if unloaded", "Allowed if it is cased", "Allowed in daylight"],
 "It is an offence to carry or possess a firearm in a public place without a lawful, proper and sufficient purpose."),
("Pointing a firearm at a person without lawful purpose, loaded or not, is:",
 "A criminal offence", ["Allowed if it is unloaded", "Only a minor breach", "Fine if done as a joke"],
 "Presenting a firearm at any person, loaded or not, except for a lawful purpose, is an offence. It also breaks Rule 2."),
("Being in charge of a firearm while affected by drink or drugs is:",
 "An offence", ["Allowed on your own land", "Allowed if you do not shoot", "Allowed under the driving limit"],
 "It is an offence to be in charge of a firearm while under the influence of drink or drugs to the extent you cannot have proper control of it."),
("Firing near a house so as to frighten people, without reasonable excuse, is:",
 "Unlawful", ["Legal on rural land", "Legal before 10 pm", "Legal if aimed away"],
 "Discharging a firearm in or near a dwelling or public place so as to endanger, annoy or frighten anyone, without reasonable excuse, is an offence."),
("You no longer want a rifle. You can sell it to:",
 "A licence holder or gun business", ["Anyone over 18 who asks", "A trusted friend without a licence", "An online buyer, unchecked"],
 "Sell or dispose of unwanted firearms only to another licence holder or a business licence holder (formerly a dealer), checking their licence first."),
]
